 weeks', 'E': 'Administer intravenous immune globulin postpartum'} \nTotal Analysis: **\nThe patient is at a high risk of vertical transmission of Group B Streptococcus (GBS) due to the presence of the organism in the rectovaginal swab culture. Given the patient's gestational age of 35 weeks, the most appropriate intervention to decrease vertical transmission of this organism is to schedule a cesarean delivery before labor and rupture of membranes. This option aligns with the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG) recommendations for preventing vertical transmission of GBS. \n"], "raw_output": "Option: A", "error": null}
